# Sprint 18 — Centralized Firewall Logging & Network Security Monitoring

## Objective

The objective of Sprint 18 was to integrate the pfSense firewall with Splunk Enterprise and establish centralized network-security monitoring for the segmented SOC home lab.

Sprint 17 introduced separate CORP-LAN and ATTACK_NET security zones protected by pfSense. Sprint 18 extended that architecture by forwarding firewall telemetry to the SIEM and using Splunk to monitor traffic crossing the security boundary.

The sprint focused on:

- Centralizing pfSense firewall logs in Splunk
- Creating a dedicated network-security index
- Configuring remote syslog between FW01 and SIEM01
- Restricting syslog ingestion at the Windows host firewall
- Validating end-to-end log delivery
- Generating known permitted and blocked traffic
- Identifying ATTACK_NET activity in Splunk
- Creating reusable security searches
- Building a Network Security Monitoring dashboard
- Validating the complete network-monitoring pipeline

