# Validation

## 1. Connectivity Validation

Before configuring remote logging, FW01 connectivity to SIEM01 was verified.

```sh
ping -c 4 10.10.10.20
```

This established that the network path between the firewall and SIEM was operational before application-layer troubleshooting began.

---

## 2. UDP Listener Validation

SIEM01 was verified to be listening for syslog traffic on UDP/5514.

```powershell
Get-NetUDPEndpoint -LocalPort 5514
```

The listener confirmed that Splunk was prepared to receive remote firewall telemetry.

---

## 3. pfSense Event Ingestion

After remote logging was enabled, Splunk was searched using:

```spl
index=network
```

pfSense events successfully appeared in the dedicated network index.

Firewall-specific activity could be identified using:

```spl
index=network filterlog
```

This confirmed the complete telemetry path:

```text
FW01 -> UDP/5514 -> SIEM01 -> Splunk -> network index
```

