# Controlled Security Testing

Known network traffic was generated from KALI01 to validate that firewall enforcement and SIEM visibility agreed.

## Blocked Traffic Test

KALI01 attempted to reach TCP/445 on a CORP-LAN system without a corresponding pfSense allow rule.

Example:

```bash
nc -vz -w 3 10.10.10.20 445
```

The traffic represented:

```text
KALI01
10.10.20.10
     |
     | TCP/445
     v
+----------+
|   FW01   |
|  BLOCK   |
+----------+
     X
     |
     v
SIEM01
10.10.10.20
```

The blocked activity was subsequently identified in Splunk.

Example search:

```spl
index=network "10.10.20.10" "10.10.10.20" "445"
```

This demonstrated that denied firewall activity was visible to the SIEM.

---

## Permitted Traffic Test

Sprint 17 established a controlled firewall exception permitting ICMP from:

```text
KALI01
10.10.20.10
```

to:

```text
WIN11-02
10.10.10.102
```

Test traffic was generated:

```bash
ping -c 4 10.10.10.102
```

The traffic successfully crossed the firewall according to the explicit security policy.

The associated firewall telemetry was then located in Splunk:

```spl
index=network "10.10.20.10" "10.10.10.102"
```

This provided visibility into both sides of firewall enforcement:

```text
Unauthorized Traffic
KALI01 -> SIEM01:445
          BLOCK

Authorized Test Traffic
KALI01 -> WIN11-02:ICMP
          PASS
```

