# ATTACK_NET Monitoring

Because KALI01 resides on the isolated ATTACK_NET, firewall telemetry can be used to monitor activity originating from the security-testing environment.

A reusable search was created:

```spl
index=network "10.10.20.10"
```

Saved Search:

```text
ATTACK_NET - All Firewall Activity
```

Purpose:

> Displays pfSense firewall events associated with the isolated ATTACK_NET security-testing host.

This provides a simple starting point for investigating traffic originating from KALI01.

---

# Blocked Traffic Monitoring

A second search was created to focus on denied ATTACK_NET activity.

```spl
index=network "10.10.20.10" "block"
```

Saved Search:

```text
ATTACK_NET - Blocked Traffic
```

This allows denied connection attempts from the attack network to be reviewed separately from permitted traffic.

