# Security Principles Demonstrated

## Centralized Logging

Firewall events are forwarded from the network security boundary to a centralized SIEM.

## Network Segmentation

ATTACK_NET remains isolated from CORP-LAN except where explicitly permitted.

## Least Privilege

The SIEM host permits UDP/5514 only from the pfSense firewall rather than the entire network.

## Defense in Depth

Security enforcement exists at both the network and endpoint layers.

## Security Visibility

Permitted and blocked network activity can be reviewed centrally in Splunk.

## Validation Through Controlled Testing

Known traffic was intentionally generated to validate that firewall policy and SIEM telemetry accurately reflected each other.

